   "question":"A snail is at the bottom of a 20-step staircase. Each day, it climbs up 3 steps, but at night, it slips back 2 steps. How many days will it take for the snail to reach the top of the staircase?",
   "options":["10 days","12 days","15 days","20 days"],
   "answerIndex":2,
   "explanation":"The snail climbs 3 steps and slips back 2 steps each day, so it effectively climbs 1 step each day. To reach the top of the staircase, it will take 18 days (20 - 2 = 18). However, the snail will reach the top on the 19th day, as it will climb 3 steps on the 19th day and reach the top."
