   "question":"A group of friends want to share some money equally. If they have $240 and there are 8 friends, but one friend is absent, how much money will each of the remaining friends get?",
   "options":["$25","$30","$35","$40"],
   "answerIndex":3,
   "explanation":"Since one friend is absent, there are 7 friends remaining. To find out how much each friend will get, we divide the total amount of money by the number of friends. 240 ÷ 7 = 34.29 (rounded to two decimal places). So, each of the remaining friends will get approximately $34.29."
