   "question":"A car travels from city A to city B at an average speed of 60 km/h. On the return trip, the car travels at an average speed of 40 km/h. If the distance between the two cities is 240 km, how long does the return trip take?",
   "options":["4 hours","5 hours","6 hours","8 hours"],
   "answerIndex":1,
   "explanation":"The distance between the two cities is 240 km. To find the time it takes to travel at an average speed of 40 km/h, we divide the distance by the speed. 240 ÷ 40 = 6 hours."
